sentences.text:
This Court has considered following aspects,
(i) as per the FIR, the complainant was abducted in December-2020, whereas FIR is registered on 7.7.2022 and why there was a delay of almost one and half year in registering the FIR is not stated by explaining the delay sufficiently in the FIR;
(ii) as per the FIR, the main accused person is Ketan Der and Husain Rafai, whereas the present applicant happens to be a family member of the main accused Ketan Der and the allegation against the present applicant is that he was one of the accused person who abducted the complainant and took her to Junagadh in December-2020.

However, learned APP could not point out that the present applicant has not R/CR.MA/16768/2022 ORDER DATED: 19/06/2023 co-operated in the investigation or that there is any other material than what has been referred to in the foregoing paragraph against the present applicant;
(v) the present applicant has shown readiness and willingness to co-operate with the investigation;
7.

The applicant is ordered to be released on bail in the event of their arrest in connection with FIR bearing C.R.No.11191030220044 of 2022 dated 7.7.2022 registered with Mahila Police Station (West), District : Ahmedabad, on executing a personal R/CR.MA/16768/2022 ORDER DATED: 19/06/2023 bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten Thousand Only) with one surety of like amount on the following conditions:
(a) shall cooperate with the investigation and make himself available for interrogation whenever required;
(b) shall remain present at concerned Police Station on 22.6.2023 between 11.00 a.m. and 2.00 p.m.;
(c) shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the fact of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the Court or to any police officer;
(d) shall not obstruct or hamper the police investigation and not to play mischief with the evidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;
 (e) shall at the time of execution of  bond, furnish the address to the  investigating officer and the Court concerned and shall not change residence till the final disposal of the case till further orders;
R/CR.MA/16768/2022 ORDER DATED: 19/06/2023 (f) shall not leave India without the permission of the concerned trial Court and if having passport shall deposit the same before the concerned trial Court within a week; and (g) it would be open to the Investigating Officer to file an application for remand if he considers it proper and just and the learned Magistrate would decide it on merits;
10.

